index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..3a32bc183013cd3bef4598d4c838a24dc23a2061
--- /dev/null
+++ b/packages/host/web-restart/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,75 @@
+# @deepseek-ai/dsh-host-web-restart
+
+Web-host restart command for the dsh web profile. Provides a plugin-owned
+`/restart` command backed by the checkout's proven one-shot Scheduled Task
+worker.
+
+## What it does
+
+- Registers the human slash command `/restart` on every session.
+- On invocation it synchronously asks `dsh-web-restart.ps1` to register and
+  start a one-shot Windows Scheduled Task BEFORE the old Host is stopped.
+- Windows owns that worker independently of the Host process. It:
+  1. waits briefly,
+  2. stops the current web Host,
+  3. waits for port 3080 to release,
+  4. relaunches `start-dsh-web.cmd`,
+  5. waits for the root page and `/api/host.describe` readiness handshake,
+  6. reopens the browser once, and
+  7. unregisters itself.
+
+The configured `start-dsh-web.cmd` launches the Host with `--no-open`, so the
+Host itself does not race the worker to open a second browser window.
+
+The host's own session persistence and the "continue task" surface then behave
+exactly as after a script-driven restart.
+
+## Configuration
+
+Mount via the web profile's `cordis.patch.yml`:
+
+```yaml
+- insert:
+    - id: web-restart
+      name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-host-web-restart'
+      config:
+        port: 3080
+        startCmd: C:\Users\19161\deepseek-harness\start-dsh-web.cmd
+        repoRoot: C:\Users\19161\deepseek-harness
+        verifyLog: C:\Users\19161\deepseek-harness\dsh-restart-verify.log
+        openBrowser: true
+```
+
+| Field | Default | Meaning |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `port` | `3080` | TCP port the web host listens on |
+| `startCmd` | required | absolute path to `start-dsh-web.cmd` |
+| `repoRoot` | required | working directory for relaunching the host |
+| `verifyLog` | absent | optional lifecycle log path |
+| `openBrowser` | `true` | reopen the browser after the host returns |
+| `stopSeconds` | `20` | seconds to wait for the old port to release |
+| `waitSeconds` | `60` | seconds to wait for the full Host readiness handshake |
+
+`startCmd` and `repoRoot` must point to the same checkout. The plugin uses the
+PowerShell scheduler script from `repoRoot`, so an external shortcut is not
+needed for `/restart`.
+
+## Layout
+
+- `src/index.ts` — plugin config, `/restart`, and Scheduled Task scheduler handoff.
+- `src/worker.ts` — retained restart/readiness helpers and tests; the installed
+  Windows command path uses `dsh-web-restart.ps1` for durable process ownership.
+- `tests/worker.spec.ts` — config and `netstat` parsing tests.
+
+## Building
+
+```sh
+pnpm exec tsc -b packages/host/web-restart
+pnpm --filter @deepseek-ai/dsh-host-web-restart bundle
+```
+
+Run tests:
+
+```sh
+pnpm exec vitest run packages/host/web-restart/tests/worker.spec.ts
+```
